    "probe_text": "I've traced the full pipeline. Here is the complete ordered list.\n\n## POST /api/owners \u2014 ordered validations and side-effects\n\n**Gate (before any step):**\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; without that role the request is denied (403) and nothing below runs.\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotency`** *(txn)*\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header (trimmed; blank treated as absent).\n- If the key was seen before *and* the previously created owner still exists \u2192 **short-circuits**: responds **200** with that existing owner and creates nothing (no duplicate, no 409). Otherwise takes the `create` flow into the rest of the pipeline.\n\n**2. `RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 the one `@RequestBody` binding\n- **Normalizes address**: `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` trimmed/collapsed, and a composed `address` is built (falling back to the flat `address`).\n- **Missing-field validation**: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank (address checked *after* normalization) \u2192 else `MissingFieldsException` (**400**).\n- **Normalizes telephone** to E.164 \u2192 invalid throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n- **Normalizes email** (may throw `InvalidEmailException`, 400).\n- Publishes the normalized body for later steps (so stored/returned/compared values are the normalized form).\n\n**3. `RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture`**\n- If a `registrationDate` is supplied and is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**). Absent date is allowed. Uses the supplied date, before any business-day roll.\n\n**4. `RequirePostcode`**\n- Only validates when a postcode is present: must be 4 digits and, for a city with a known region, within that region's range \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**). Absent postcode passes.\n\n**5. `RequireUniqueIdentity`** *(txn)* \u2014 scans all owners (skipping soft-deleted)\n- **Contact-key collision** (matching telephone + email) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**), regardless of `sharesHousehold`.\n- **Household collision** (same last name + postcode) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**), *unless* the request set `sharesHousehold` (which bypasses only this household check).\n\n**6. `RequireCityCapacity`** *(txn)*\n- Rejects if the owner's city (case-insensitive, trimmed) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n**7. `RequireDailyRegistrationLimit`** *(txn)*\n- Computes the effective registration date rolled forward off weekends to Monday; rejects if \u2265 100 owners already have that business day \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitException` (**429**).\n\n**8. `BuildOwner`** *(txn)* \u2014 first mutation step\n- Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity and **sets `registrationDate` to the business-day-adjusted date** (weekend \u2192 next Monday).\n\n**9. `FlagPossibleDuplicate`** *(txn)*\n- Sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`: `true` + earliest matching owner id when it shares an existing owner's last name + postcode but has a *different* telephone (and isn't a declared household member). A `sharesHousehold` member is never flagged. Soft-deleted owners ignored.\n\n**10. `AssignCustomerCode`** *(txn)*\n- Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256 of normalized telephone + last name), appending `-<n>` (n \u2265 2) if it collides with an existing code.\n\n**11. `CountNamesakes`** *(txn)*\n- Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), counted before this owner is saved.\n\n**12. `CountHouseholdMembers`** *(txn)*\n- Sets `householdSize` = existing household members (same last name + postcode) **+ 1** for this owner.\n\n**13. `FlagBulkSignupWarning`** *(txn)*\n- Sets `bulkSignupWarning` = `true` if > 80 owners already share this owner's adjusted registration date.\n\n**14. `SaveOwner`** *(txn)*\n- **Persists** the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (assigns its generated id).\n\n**15. `RecordIdempotency`** *(txn)*\n- If the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, **records** key \u2192 new owner id in the idempotency store (so a later repeat returns this owner).\n\n**16. `AuditOwnerCreated`** *(txn)*\n- **Logs** a line to the `AUDIT` logger with id, customerCode, registrationDate, computed membershipLevel and membershipNumber (derived at log time; not stored).\n\n**17. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(txn)*\n- Responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the owner DTO body.\n\n**Notes:**\n- Every step from `check` onward runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all the reads/mutations/save commit as a single transaction at the end.\n- Escalation handlers map each exception to its status (e.g. `NotFoundException`, `DataIntegrityViolationException`, and the owner-specific exceptions above); anything unmatched falls through to Spring's advice.\n- Steps 3\u20134 validate against the supplied date/postcode; the daily-limit (7) and build (8) use the *business-day-adjusted* date."
